t/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src","raw_input":"{\"pattern\":\"new PhaseOneAssessment\\\\(\",\"path\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-n\":true}","input":{"pattern":"new PhaseOneAssessment\\(","path":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src","output_mode":"content","-n":true},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_20801fdfa68b4e35b71a19b7","name":"grep -l \"PhaseOneAssessment[^R]\" /Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java","raw_input":"{\"pattern\":\"PhaseOneAssessment[^R]\",\"path\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java\",\"output_mode\":\"files_with_matches\"}","input":{"pattern":"PhaseOneAssessment[^R]","path":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java","output_mode":"files_with_matches"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"Thinking":{"text":"I've confirmed:\n- `new PhaseOneAssessment(` only appears at PhaseOneAssessmentService.java:112 — the only construction point.\n- Consumers: DecisionWorkbenchController (web, read-only, doesn't construct), AssessIncomeCliRunner (CLI), the record itself, and the service.\n\nI need to check whether DecisionWorkbenchController constructs via positional access or uses accessor — it only consumes via accessors, and the record change adds a component, which doesn't break accessor-based consumers. Adding a record component changes the canonical constructor signature, but only the service constructs it. Good.\n\nOne thing to check: does DecisionWorkbenchController or any code use the record's accessor by ordinal (e.g., reflection)? Unlikely. Design says CLI 与 DecisionWorkbenchController 只经服务评估并按访问器只读消费 — verified as design fact.\n\nNow I have everything to write the plan. The plan needs:\n\n- `implementation_steps`: ordered implementation steps- `edit_files`: canonical proposed paths (6 files)\n- `reference_files`: files referenced (PhaseOneAssessmentRequest.java, SmartArbitrageCosts.java, docs/09, docs/README.md, task-contract)\n- `file_level_changes`: path: intended change- `validation_plan`: verification commands/checks (to be run by self-test node later)\n- `rollback_notes`\n- `known_risks`\n- `human_review_checklist`\n- `files`: [{path, operation}]\n- `verification_bindings`: array with criterion_id, method, executor, environment_refs, authority_refs, evidence_kind, feasibility_refs, detail_owner, actual_exit_required, expected_exit_code- `authority_refs`\n\nFor verification_bindings, I should bind TR-1..TR-4 (the approved test requirements) and maybe AC criteria. The criterion_id should be \"approved-criterion-id\" — the approved criteria are AC-1..AC-5 and TR-1..TR-4 from the task contract. Let me create bindings for TR-1 through TR-4 (the test requirements own execution evidence), each with:\n- method: observable assertion and execution method (e.g., `mvn -pl ... test -Dtest=PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest` — actually it's a single-module Maven project; commands: `mvn test -Dtest=PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest` etc.)\n- executor: \"AGENT\"\n- environment_refs: needs ref + sha256. The environment ref — what environment? The fixed isolated baseline (branch codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026 @7c5facc). I don't have a sha256 for it readily; I could compute the commit sha... but sha256 field expects a sha256 hash. Hmm. The template says `\"ref\" : \"replace/with/actual-environment-ref\", \"sha256\" : \"0000...\"`.For environment_refs, I can reference the git commit7c5facc as the fixed baseline. The sha256 — I can't run commands (planning boundary: read/search tools only — actually the boundary says \"You may inspect context and repository files using read/search tools only\"). So I cannot run `git rev-parse` or `sha256sum`. Hmm. Can I read .git files? Reading .git/refs/heads/... would give me the commit hash (sha1). The sha256 field — maybe I can use the commit hash padded? No — should not fabricate.\n\nOptions: leave environment_refs empty array? The contract says each verification_binding must explicitly set actual_exit_required and expected_exit_code; environment_refs is an array — could be empty. But better to provide meaningful refs. The requirement statement says \"Each verification_binding must explicitly set actual_exit_required (boolean) and expected_exit_code (integer or null).\" It doesn't mandate non-empty arrays for environment_refs.\n\nHowever, the template example shows environment_refs with a ref+sha256. For honesty, I can reference the baseline commit via its ref path like \"git:codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026@7c5facc\" — but sha256 would need to be the actual sha256 of something. The git commit object is sha1, not sha256.\n\nAlternative: reference the task contract file `.agent/workstreams/.../task-contract.md` — but that's an .agent path; the constraint \"must not contain `.agent` segments\" applies to edit_files scope paths (\"Each scope path must name one ex...","signature":null}},{"Text":"{\"schema_version\":1,\"workstream_id\":\"ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA\",\"run_id\":\"run-1793030521008\",\"node_id\":\"plan.claude_plan\",\"result\":{\"artifact_type\":\"plan_result\",\"decision\":\"READY_FOR_PLAN_REVIEW\",\"summary\":\"已将复审通过的设计转为六文件实现计划：服务计算追平阈值、record承载、CLI 只读展示、两份测试与一份中文说明，程序化验证交由自测节点执行。\",\"lifecycle_status\":\"READY\",\"blocking\":false,\"checks\":[\"已读取经评审通过的设计（run-1793029979831 design-claude.contract.json，decision=READY_FOR_ARCH_REVIEW）与 Codex复审（run-1793030419328，mustFix 为空），R1/R2修订均已纳入